{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_master_key_rotation_master_key_rotation", "label": "Master key rotation", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Rotation is online: new writes go under the active key, old reads dispatch on the version byte in each blob manifest, and a background sweep eventually moves the corpus.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/master-key-rotation.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_master_key_rotation_masterkeyring", "label": "MasterKeyRing", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A type, not a class: one active key plus any number of retired ones, each 32 raw bytes tagged with a numeric version. You build the plain object; there is nothing to new.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/master-key-rotation.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_master_key_rotation_version_byte", "label": "One-byte key version uniqueness", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The version byte is the reader only handle on the key, so duplicate versions are rejected at registration, at the store and at sweep start. The byte caps how many versions are live at once, not how often you rotate; registration warns from 240 on.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/master-key-rotation.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_master_key_rotation_rotation_flow", "label": "Five-step online rotation flow", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Add the key as retired, roll out, promote it to active, run the sweep, then drop the old key after a rollback window. Every step is supported without downtime.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/master-key-rotation.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_master_key_rotation_reencryptobjectstorage", "label": "reEncryptObjectStorage sweep", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Lists every object under keyPrefix and re-encrypts anything not at the ring active version; idempotent and resumable. info must be the exact HKDF context the encrypting store uses, or every decrypt fails rather than silently producing wrong output.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/master-key-rotation.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_master_key_rotation_verifykeyringcompleteness", "label": "verifyKeyringCompleteness", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "On by default: samples blobs and refuses to start if any references a version missing from the ring, catching the dropped-retired-key footgun before the sweep writes a single object.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/master-key-rotation.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_master_key_rotation_rollback_window", "label": "Rollback window before retiring a key", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Nothing guards the live read path, so data still under a dropped key becomes permanently unreadable; keep the old key about seven days past sweep completion in case the sweep missed backups.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/master-key-rotation.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_master_key_rotation_key_storage_patterns", "label": "Master key storage patterns", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Env vars are visible to anything that can read the process environment; KMS is the production answer, so the environment holds only a reference and keys never leave the secure boundary in plaintext.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/master-key-rotation.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_master_key_rotation_sweep_has_no_throttle", "label": "The sweep has no built-in throttle", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "There is no rateLimit or batchSize knob, so a large sweep competes with foreground traffic and runs up S3 request costs; scope it with keyPrefix and skip, run it off-peak, and bias toward not impacting production.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/master-key-rotation.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_master_key_rotation_multi_cluster_keyring", "label": "Multi-cluster keyring alignment", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Clusters sharing one encrypted store, such as a DR replica reading the primary backups, all need the same ring; rotate them together so none falls behind on key generations.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/master-key-rotation.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_master_key_rotation_master_key_rotation", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_master_key_rotation_masterkeyring", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/master-key-rotation.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_conte